<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A German XRechnung sent in the CII syntax — the other binding EN 16931 allows,
  and the one Factur-X/ZUGFeRD carries inside a PDF.

  Deliberately exercises what differs from UBL:
    - YYYYMMDD dates behind udt:DateTimeString format="102"
    - no per-amount currencyID; the currency is stated once
    - the seller VAT number qualified by schemeID="VA"
    - a document-level allowance with ChargeIndicator nested in udt:Indicator
    - CII's own names for the totals (GrandTotalAmount = BT-112)

  Figures: 2 lines at 19% (800.00 + 200.00 net), 50.00 invoice discount,
  so 950.00 net, 180.50 VAT, 1130.50 gross.
-->
